2025-05-01 03:41:57 - Thread-1601 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Relevant columns and their potential usages  
• "NFIP_COMMUNITY_NAME": name of the community that filed the claim – filter to “City Of New York”.  
• "DATE_OF_LOSS": the date the flood loss occurred – extract the loss year (2010‑2019) and use it for grouping.  
• "BUILDING_DAMAGE_AMOUNT": dollar amount of damage to the building – aggregate with SUM() for each year.  
• "CONTENTS_DAMAGE_AMOUNT": dollar amount of damage to the contents – aggregate with SUM() for each year.  

Below are ten exploratory‑to‑final Snowflake SQL queries (enclose all identifiers in double quotes) that progressively investigate the data and finally produce the yearly totals. Each returns at most 20 rows for inspection.

```sql
-- 1. Description: View a few distinct NFIP community names to confirm naming conventions.
SELECT DISTINCT "NFIP_COMMUNITY_NAME"
FROM "WEATHER__ENVIRONMENT"."CYBERSYN"."FEMA_NATIONAL_FLOOD_INSURANCE_PROGRAM_CLAIM_INDEX"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Fuzzy search to make sure “City Of New York” appears exactly as expected.
SELECT DISTINCT "NFIP_COMMUNITY_NAME"
FROM "WEATHER__ENVIRONMENT"."CYBERSYN"."FEMA_NATIONAL_FLOOD_INSURANCE_PROGRAM_CLAIM_INDEX"
WHERE "NFIP_COMMUNITY_NAME" ILIKE '%city%of%new%york%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Peek at a few claims for the City of New York with their dates of loss.
SELECT "NATIONAL_FLOOD_INSURANCE_PROGRAM_CLAIM_ID",
       "DATE_OF_LOSS",
       "BUILDING_DAMAGE_AMOUNT",
       "CONTENTS_DAMAGE_AMOUNT"
FROM "WEATHER__ENVIRONMENT"."CYBERSYN"."FEMA_NATIONAL_FLOOD_INSURANCE_PROGRAM_CLAIM_INDEX"
WHERE "NFIP_COMMUNITY_NAME" = 'City Of New York'
ORDER BY "DATE_OF_LOSS"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Check min and max loss dates for the City of New York.
SELECT MIN("DATE_OF_LOSS") AS "earliest_loss",
       MAX("DATE_OF_LOSS") AS "latest_loss"
FROM "WEATHER__ENVIRONMENT"."CYBERSYN"."FEMA_NATIONAL_FLOOD_INSURANCE_PROGRAM_CLAIM_INDEX"
WHERE "NFIP_COMMUNITY_NAME" = 'City Of New York';
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Count number of claims by year (all years) for the City of New York.
SELECT EXTRACT(YEAR FROM "DATE_OF_LOSS") AS "loss_year",
       COUNT(*) AS "claim_count"
FROM "WEATHER__ENVIRONMENT"."CYBERSYN"."FEMA_NATIONAL_FLOOD_INSURANCE_PROGRAM_CLAIM_INDEX"
WHERE "NFIP_COMMUNITY_NAME" = 'City Of New York'
GROUP BY "loss_year"
ORDER BY "loss_year"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Yearly total building damage (all years) for the City of New York.
SELECT EXTRACT(YEAR FROM "DATE_OF_LOSS") AS "loss_year",
       SUM("BUILDING_DAMAGE_AMOUNT") AS "total_building_damage_usd"
FROM "WEATHER__ENVIRONMENT"."CYBERSYN"."FEMA_NATIONAL_FLOOD_INSURANCE_PROGRAM_CLAIM_INDEX"
WHERE "NFIP_COMMUNITY_NAME" = 'City Of New York'
GROUP BY "loss_year"
ORDER BY "loss_year"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Yearly total contents damage (all years) for the City of New York.
SELECT EXTRACT(YEAR FROM "DATE_OF_LOSS") AS "loss_year",
       SUM("CONTENTS_DAMAGE_AMOUNT") AS "total_contents_damage_usd"
FROM "WEATHER__ENVIRONMENT"."CYBERSYN"."FEMA_NATIONAL_FLOOD_INSURANCE_PROGRAM_CLAIM_INDEX"
WHERE "NFIP_COMMUNITY_NAME" = 'City Of New York'
GROUP BY "loss_year"
ORDER BY "loss_year"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Combine building and contents totals for ALL years in one query.
SELECT EXTRACT(YEAR FROM "DATE_OF_LOSS") AS "loss_year",
       SUM("BUILDING_DAMAGE_AMOUNT") AS "total_building_damage_usd",
       SUM("CONTENTS_DAMAGE_AMOUNT") AS "total_contents_damage_usd"
FROM "WEATHER__ENVIRONMENT"."CYBERSYN"."FEMA_NATIONAL_FLOOD_INSURANCE_PROGRAM_CLAIM_INDEX"
WHERE "NFIP_COMMUNITY_NAME" = 'City Of New York'
GROUP BY "loss_year"
ORDER BY "loss_year"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Same as #8 but restricted to 2010‑2019 inclusive.
SELECT EXTRACT(YEAR FROM "DATE_OF_LOSS") AS "loss_year",
       SUM("BUILDING_DAMAGE_AMOUNT") AS "total_building_damage_usd",
       SUM("CONTENTS_DAMAGE_AMOUNT") AS "total_contents_damage_usd"
FROM "WEATHER__ENVIRONMENT"."CYBERSYN"."FEMA_NATIONAL_FLOOD_INSURANCE_PROGRAM_CLAIM_INDEX"
WHERE "NFIP_COMMUNITY_NAME" = 'City Of New York'
  AND "DATE_OF_LOSS" BETWEEN '2010-01-01' AND '2019-12-31'
GROUP BY "loss_year"
ORDER BY "loss_year"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: Final aggregated answer query – yearly totals 2010‑2019, ordered chronologically.
SELECT EXTRACT(YEAR FROM "DATE_OF_LOSS") AS "loss_year",
       SUM("BUILDING_DAMAGE_AMOUNT") :: NUMBER(38,2) AS "total_building_damage_usd",
       SUM("CONTENTS_DAMAGE_AMOUNT") :: NUMBER(38,2) AS "total_contents_damage_usd"
FROM "WEATHER__ENVIRONMENT"."CYBERSYN"."FEMA_NATIONAL_FLOOD_INSURANCE_PROGRAM_CLAIM_INDEX"
WHERE "NFIP_COMMUNITY_NAME" = 'City Of New York'
  AND "DATE_OF_LOSS" >= '2010-01-01'
  AND "DATE_OF_LOSS" <  '2020-01-01'
GROUP BY "loss_year"
ORDER BY "loss_year";
```
