Table full name: WEATHER__ENVIRONMENT.CYBERSYN.FEMA_NATIONAL_FLOOD_INSURANCE_PROGRAM_CLAIM_INDEX
Column name: LATITUDE Type: FLOAT Description: Latitude of the insured property.
Column name: ICC_COVERAGE Type: NUMBER Description: Amount of Increased Cost of Compliance (ICC) coverage for building in whole dollars. ICC coverage is the coverage for expenses that a property owner must incur, above and beyond the cost to repair the physical damage the building actually sustained from a flooding event, to comply with mitigation requirements of state or local floodplain management ordinances or laws.
Column name: REPLACEMENT_COST_BASIS Type: TEXT Description: This indicates whether the building claim was settled on a replacement cost basis.
Column name: ORIGINAL_FLOOD_POLICY_DATE Type: DATE Description: Original date of the flood policy.
Column name: DISASTER_ASSISTANCE_COVERAGE_REQUIRED Type: TEXT Description: Federal agency that has required the purchase of flood insurance as a requirement for disaster assistance.
Column name: ELEVATION_DIFFERENCE Type: NUMBER Description: Difference between the elevation of the lowest floor used for rating, or the flood-proofed elevation, and the base flood elevation (BFE), or base flood depth, as appropriate.
Column name: EVENT_DESIGNATION_NUMBER Type: TEXT Description: The Event Designation Number (EDN) is a unique identifier established for a catastrophe flood event. EDN has replaced FICO as the new event tracking designation. Prior to June 2020 flood events were assigned FICO number designations; after June 2020, flood events are assigned EDN number designations.
Column name: FLOOD_TYPE Type: TEXT Description: Description of the characteristics of the flood.
Column name: COMMUNITY_RATING_SYSTEM_CLASS Type: TEXT Description: Community Rating System (CRS) Classification Credit Percentage used to rate the policy. The insurance premium credit is based on whether a property is in or out of the Special Flood Hazard Area (SFHA) as shown on the community's Flood Insurance Rate Map.
Column name: PROPERTY_INDICATORS Type: ARRAY Description: Array of characteristics of the insured property.
Column name: NFIP_COMMUNITY_NUMBER_CURRENT Type: TEXT Description: 6-digit designation identifying the current NFIP community. The first two numbers are the state code. The next four are the FEMA-assigned community number.
Column name: AMOUNT_PAID_ON_BUILDING_CLAIM Type: FLOAT Description: Dollar amount paid on the building claim. In some instances, a negative amount may appear which occurs when a check issued to a policy holder is not cashed and has to be re-issued.
Column name: CENSUS_TRACT_ID Type: TEXT Description: Cybersyn's unique identifier for a census tract, joinable to GEOGRAPHY_INDEX.
Column name: LONGITUDE Type: FLOAT Description: Longitude of the insured property.
Column name: FLOOD_EVENT Type: TEXT Description: Name given to a flooding catastrophe.
Column name: BUILDING_DAMAGE_AMOUNT Type: FLOAT Description: Actual cash value amount of damage to a main property in whole dollars.
Column name: CENSUS_BLOCK_GROUP_ID Type: TEXT Description: Cybersyn's unique identifier for a census block group, joinable to GEOGRAPHY_INDEX.
Column name: FLOOD_WATER_DEPTH Type: NUMBER Description: Depth of flood water in inches. There are instances where measurements were provided in feet.
Column name: AMOUNT_PAID_ON_CONTENTS_CLAIM Type: FLOAT Description: Dollar amount paid on the contents claim. In some instances, a negative amount may appear, which occurs when a check issued to a policy holder is not cashed and has to be re-issued.
Column name: FICO_NUMBER Type: NUMBER Description: Number assigned by the Flood Insurance Claims Office (FICO) at the time of a significant flooding event to uniquely identify each affected state.
Column name: BUILDING_REPLACEMENT_COST Type: NUMBER Description: Estimated cost in whole dollars to replace the building as reported by the insurer. Replacement cost is not market value, and it does not include the cost of the land or contents. It is strictly the estimated cost to reconstruct the building.
Column name: NUMBER_OF_FLOORS Type: TEXT Description: Number of floors in the insured building.
Column name: CURRENT_FLOOD_ZONE Type: TEXT Description: Flood zone derived from the Flood Insurance Rate Map (FIRM) where the insured property is currently located.
Column name: ORIGINAL_CONSTRUCTION_DATE Type: DATE Description: Original date of the construction of the building.
Column name: TOTAL_BUILDING_INSURANCE_COVERAGE Type: NUMBER Description: Total Insurance Amount in whole dollars on the Building.
Column name: NET_BUILDING_PAYMENT_AMOUNT Type: FLOAT Description: Net building payment amount made to insured in dollars.
Column name: NFIP_RATED_COMMUNITY_NUMBER Type: TEXT Description: 6-digit designation identifying the rated NFIP community. The first two numbers are the state code. The next four are the FEMA-assigned community number.
Column name: BUILDING_PROPERTY_VALUE Type: NUMBER Description: Actual cash value of the main building in whole dollars as estimated by an adjuster.
Column name: TOTAL_CONTENTS_INSURANCE_COVERAGE Type: NUMBER Description: Total Insurance Amount in whole dollars on the Contents.
Column name: CONDOMINIUM_COVERAGE_TYPE Type: TEXT Description: Type of coverage the building has if it is a condominium.
Column name: BASE_FLOOD_ELEVATION Type: FLOAT Description: Base Flood Elevation (BFE) is the elevation in feet from the Elevation Certificate at which there is a 1% chance per year of flooding.
Column name: NFIP_COMMUNITY_NAME Type: TEXT Description: Local political entity that has the authority to adopt and enforce floodplain ordinances for the area under its jurisdiction.
Column name: CAUSE_OF_DAMAGE Type: TEXT Description: The method by which the insured's property and contents were damaged.
Column name: NON_PAYMENT_REASON_CONTENTS Type: TEXT Description: Reason why a claim was not paid for the contents of a property.
Column name: POLICY_COUNT Type: NUMBER Description: Insured units in an active status. A policy contract ceases to be in an active status as of the cancellation date or the expiration date. Residential Condominium Building Association Policy (RCBAP) contracts are stored as a single policy contract but insure multiple units and therefore represent multiple policies.
Column name: POLICY_RATING_METHOD Type: TEXT Description: Policy rating method.
Column name: OBSTRUCTION Type: TEXT Description: Type of obstruction in the enclosure of the insured property.
Column name: ZIP_GEO_ID Type: TEXT Description: Cybersyn's unique identifier for a zip code, joinable to GEOGRAPHY_INDEX.
Column name: POLICY_RATED_FLOOD_ZONE Type: TEXT Description: Formerly called floodZone. NFIP Flood Zone derived from the Flood Insurance Rate Map (FIRM) used to rate the insured property.
Column name: CITY Type: TEXT Description: City of the insured property.
Column name: NATIONAL_FLOOD_INSURANCE_PROGRAM_CLAIM_ID Type: TEXT Description: Unique record identifier from FEMA for the claim.
Column name: BASEMENT_ENCLOSURE_CRAWLSPACE Type: TEXT Description: Basement is defined for purposes of the NFIP as any level or story which has its floor sub-grade on all sides.
Column name: NET_CONTENTS_PAYMENT_AMOUNT Type: FLOAT Description: Net contents payment amount made to insured in dollars.
Column name: LOWEST_FLOOR_ELEVATION Type: FLOAT Description: A building's lowest floor is the floor or level (including basement/enclosure/crawlspace/sub-grade crawlspace) that is used as the point of reference when rating a building. This includes the level to which a building is flood-proofed. The elevation in feet of the reference level of the building from the Elevation Certificate.
Column name: OCCUPANCY_TYPE Type: TEXT Description: Description of the use and occupancy type of the insured structure.
Column name: UNITS Type: NUMBER Description: The number of residential and nonresidential units covered by the Condominium Master Policy.
Column name: NON_PAYMENT_REASON_BUILDING Type: TEXT Description: Reason why a claim was not paid for a property structure.
Column name: CONTENTS_DEDUCTIBLE Type: NUMBER Description: Total deductible amount in dollars for contents in both main and apartment structures that can be applied against the loss.
Column name: CONTENT_LOCATION Type: TEXT Description: The location of the contents of the property.
Column name: FLOOD_WATER_DURATION_HOURS Type: NUMBER Description: Number of hours flood water remained in the insured building.
Column name: DATE_OF_LOSS Type: DATE Description: Date on which water first entered the insured building.
Column name: BUILDING_TYPE Type: TEXT Description: Description of the use of the insured building.
Column name: CONTENTS_DAMAGE_AMOUNT Type: FLOAT Description: Actual cash value amount of damage to contents in whole dollars.
Column name: COUNTY_GEO_ID Type: TEXT Description: Cybersyn's unique identifier for a county, joinable to GEOGRAPHY_INDEX.
Column name: NET_ICC_PAYMENT_AMOUNT Type: FLOAT Description: Net Increased Cost of Compliance (ICC) payment amount made to insured in dollars.
Column name: CONTENTS_PROPERTY_VALUE Type: NUMBER Description: Actual cash value of the contents in whole dollars as estimated by an adjuster.
Column name: CONTENTS_REPLACEMENT_COST Type: NUMBER Description: Estimated cost in whole dollars to replace the contents as reported by the insurer. Replacement cost is not market value, and it does not include the cost of the land or building. It is strictly the estimated cost to replace the contents.
Column name: AMOUNT_PAID_ON_INCREASED_COST_OF_COMPLIANCE_CLAIM Type: FLOAT Description: ICC coverage is one of several flood insurance resources for policyholders who need additional help rebuilding after a flood. It provides up to $30,000 to help cover the cost of mitigation measures that will reduce the flood risk.
Column name: LOWEST_ADJACENT_GRADE Type: FLOAT Description: Lowest natural grade adjacent to the insured structure prior to excavating or filling. The difference in feet of the lowest natural grade adjacent to the building from the reference level of the building.
Column name: BUILDING_DEDUCTIBLE Type: NUMBER Description: Total deductible amount in dollars for buildings, both main and appurtenant, that can be applied against a loss.
Column name: STATE_GEO_ID Type: TEXT Description: Cybersyn's unique identifier for a state, joinable to GEOGRAPHY_INDEX.
Sample rows:
[{'NATIONAL_FLOOD_INSURANCE_PROGRAM_CLAIM_ID': '183de939-7a59-4437-b443-24531077c464', 'BUILDING_TYPE': 'Main House', 'OCCUPANCY_TYPE': 'Single family residence', 'UNITS': 1, 'EVENT_DESIGNATION_NUMBER': None, 'FICO_NUMBER': 679.0, 'FLOOD_EVENT': 'Mid-summer severe storms', 'FLOOD_TYPE': None, 'FLOOD_WATER_DURATION_HOURS': 0, 'FLOOD_WATER_DEPTH': 1, 'CAUSE_OF_DAMAGE': 'Accumulation of rainfall or snowmelt', 'DATE_OF_LOSS': '2016-08-13', 'BUILDING_PROPERTY_VALUE': 183144.0, 'BUILDING_DAMAGE_AMOUNT': 64878.0, 'AMOUNT_PAID_ON_BUILDING_CLAIM': 40000.0, 'NET_BUILDING_PAYMENT_AMOUNT': 40000.0, 'NON_PAYMENT_REASON_BUILDING': None, 'CONTENTS_PROPERTY_VALUE': 0.0, 'CONTENTS_DAMAGE_AMOUNT': 19500.0, 'CONTENTS_REPLACEMENT_COST': 0.0, 'AMOUNT_PAID_ON_CONTENTS_CLAIM': 10000.0, 'NET_CONTENTS_PAYMENT_AMOUNT': 10000.0, 'NON_PAYMENT_REASON_CONTENTS': None, 'AMOUNT_PAID_ON_INCREASED_COST_OF_COMPLIANCE_CLAIM': 0.0, 'ICC_COVERAGE': 30000.0, 'NET_ICC_PAYMENT_AMOUNT': 0.0, 'REPLACEMENT_COST_BASIS': 'Actual C


