Table full name: WEATHER__ENVIRONMENT.CYBERSYN.FEMA_NATIONAL_FLOOD_INSURANCE_PROGRAM_POLICY_INDEX
Column name: LATITUDE Type: FLOAT Description: Latitude of the insured property.
Column name: LONGITUDE Type: FLOAT Description: Longitude of the insured property.
Column name: ORIGINAL_FLOOD_POLICY_DATE Type: DATE Description: Original date of the flood policy.
Column name: POLICY_RATED_FLOOD_ZONE Type: TEXT Description: Formerly called floodZone. NFIP Flood Zone derived from the Flood Insurance Rate Map (FIRM) used to rate the insured property.
Column name: ELEVATION_DIFFERENCE Type: NUMBER Description: Difference between the elevation of the lowest floor used for rating, or the flood-proofed elevation, and the base flood elevation (BFE), or base flood depth, as appropriate.
Column name: SUBSIDIZATION_TYPE Type: TEXT Description: Type of rate subsidization received on the policy.
Column name: PROBATION_SURCHARGE Type: NUMBER Description: The probation surcharge amount, in whole dollars, is calculated by the company to rate the policy. A probation surcharge is a flat surcharge that the policyholder must pay on each new or renewed policy issued covering property in a community that the NFIP has placed on probation under the provisions of 44 CFR 59.24
Column name: PROPERTY_PURCHASE_DATE Type: DATE Description: Date that the insured property was purchased.
Column name: TOTAL_INSURANCE_PREMIUM_OF_THE_POLICY Type: NUMBER Description: Total Insurance Premium of the Policy in whole dollars. Negative values indicate a refund.
Column name: STATE_GEO_ID Type: TEXT Description: Cybersyn's unique identifier for a state, joinable to GEOGRAPHY_INDEX.
Column name: BASEMENT_ENCLOSURE_CRAWLSPACE Type: TEXT Description: Basement is defined for purposes of the NFIP as any level or story which has its floor sub-grade on all sides.
Column name: ICC_PREMIUM Type: NUMBER Description: The whole dollar amount of the Increased Cost of Compliance (ICC) premium selected before any discounts are applied by the company to rate the policy.
Column name: NFIP_RATED_COMMUNITY_NUMBER Type: TEXT Description: 6-digit designation identifying the rated NFIP community. The first two numbers are the state code. The next four are the FEMA-assigned community number.
Column name: CONTENTS_DEDUCTIBLE Type: NUMBER Description: The total deductible amount in dollars for contents in both main and apartment structures that can be applied against the loss.
Column name: ADDITIONAL_CONTENTS_RATE Type: FLOAT Description: Additional contents rate selected by the company. This data element must be reported for all policies except the Preferred Risk Policy (PRP).
Column name: LOWEST_ADJACENT_GRADE Type: FLOAT Description: Lowest natural grade adjacent to the insured structure prior to excavating or filling. The difference in feet of the lowest natural grade adjacent to the building from the reference level of the building.
Column name: GRANDFATHERING Type: TEXT Description: Type of grandfathering, if applicable, in place for rating.
Column name: HFIAA_SURCHARGE Type: NUMBER Description: Required for all new and renewal policies on or after April 1, 2015. Congressionally mandated annual surcharge in dollars required by the Homeowner Flood Insurance Affordability Act of 2014 (HFIAA).
Column name: CITY Type: TEXT Description: City of the insured property.
Column name: ROLLOVER_TRANSFER Type: TEXT Description: Type of new business being reported by the company.
Column name: POLICY_EFFECTIVE_DATE Type: DATE Description: The effective date of the flood policy.
Column name: BUILDING_DEDUCTIBLE Type: NUMBER Description: The total deductible amount in dollars for buildings, both main and appurtenant, that can be applied against a loss.
Column name: TOTAL_BUILDING_INSURANCE_COVERAGE Type: NUMBER Description: Total Insurance Amount in whole dollars on the Building.
Column name: POLICY_TERMINATION_DATE Type: DATE Description: Date upon which the cancellation of a flood insurance policy becomes effective - either because it was cancelled or lapsed.
Column name: POLICY_CANCELLATION_REASON Type: TEXT Description: Reason for the cancellation of the policy.
Column name: MAP_PANEL_NUMBER Type: TEXT Description: Either the current map panel number for the property or the map panel number being used for rating, depending on MapInfo Type.
Column name: WAITING_PERIOD_TYPE Type: TEXT Description: Type of waiting period used to issue the policy.
Column name: TOTAL_CONTENTS_INSURANCE_COVERAGE Type: NUMBER Description: Total Insurance Amount in whole dollars on the Contents.
Column name: BASIC_CONTENTS_RATE Type: FLOAT Description: Basic contents rate selected by the company. This data element must be reported for all policies with exception of Preferred Risk Policy (PRP).
Column name: RESERVE_FUND_ASSESSMENT Type: NUMBER Description: The dollar sum of the reserve fund as reported by the company.
Column name: FEMA_REGION_ID Type: NUMBER Description: The FEMA Region number.
Column name: POLICY_CANCELLATION_DATE Type: DATE Description: The cancellation date of the flood policy (if any); date the flood policy goes out of force.
Column name: POLICY_RATING_METHOD Type: TEXT Description: Policy rating method.
Column name: BASE_FLOOD_ELEVATION Type: FLOAT Description: Base Flood Elevation (BFE) is the elevation in feet from the Elevation Certificate at which there is a 1% chance per year of flooding.
Column name: FEDERAL_POLICY_FEE Type: NUMBER Description: Dollar amount of the Federal Policy Fee of the policy.
Column name: OCCUPANCY_TYPE Type: TEXT Description: Description of the use and occupancy type of the insured structure.
Column name: POLICY_COUNT Type: NUMBER Description: Insured units in an active status. A policy contract ceases to be in an active status as of the cancellation date or the expiration date. Residential Condominium Building Association Policy (RCBAP) contracts are stored as a single policy contract but insure multiple units and therefore represent multiple policies.
Column name: NATIONAL_FLOOD_INSURANCE_PROGRAM_POLICY_ID Type: TEXT Description: Unique record identifier from FEMA for the policy.
Column name: ENDORSEMENT_EFFECTIVE_DATE Type: DATE Description: Date that a policy endorsement goes into effect.
Column name: CENSUS_TRACT_ID Type: TEXT Description: Cybersyn's unique identifier for a census tract, joinable to GEOGRAPHY_INDEX.
Column name: NFIP_COMMUNITY_NUMBER_CURRENT Type: TEXT Description: 6-digit designation identifying the current NFIP community. The first two numbers are the state code. The next four are the FEMA-assigned community number.
Column name: COUNTY_GEO_ID Type: TEXT Description: Cybersyn's unique identifier for a county, joinable to GEOGRAPHY_INDEX.
Column name: CENSUS_BLOCK_GROUP_ID Type: TEXT Description: Cybersyn's unique identifier for a census block group, joinable to GEOGRAPHY_INDEX.
Column name: POLICY_COST Type: FLOAT Description: Calculated in dollars by adding together calculated premium, reserve fund assessment, federal policy fee, and HFIAA surcharge.
Column name: NUMBER_OF_FLOORS Type: TEXT Description: Number of floors in the insured building.
Column name: PROPERTY_INDICATORS Type: ARRAY Description: Array of characteristics of the insured property.
Column name: BUILDING_REPLACEMENT_COST Type: NUMBER Description: Estimated cost in whole dollars to replace the building as reported by the insurer. Replacement cost is not market value, and it does not include the cost of the land or contents. It is strictly the estimated cost to reconstruct the building.
Column name: BASIC_BUILDING_RATE Type: FLOAT Description: Basic building rate selected by the company. This data element must be reported for all policies with exception of Preferred Risk Policy (PRP).
Column name: ENCLOSURE Type: TEXT Description: Type of enclosure below the lowest elevated floor of an elevated building, and if there is whether it is a full or partial enclosure.
Column name: DISASTER_ASSISTANCE_COVERAGE_REQUIRED Type: TEXT Description: Federal agency that has required the purchase of flood insurance as a requirement for disaster assistance.
Column name: INSURANCE_TO_VALUE_RATIO Type: TEXT Description: Ratio of building insurance coverage purchased to the replacement cost value of the building.
Column name: COMMUNITY_RATING_SYSTEM_CLASS Type: TEXT Description: Community Rating System (CRS) Classification Credit Percentage used to rate the policy. The insurance premium credit is based on whether a property is in or out of the Special Flood Hazard Area (SFHA) as shown on the community's Flood Insurance Rate Map.
Column name: BUILDING_TYPE Type: TEXT Description: Description of the use of the insured building.
Column name: NFIP_COMMUNITY_NAME Type: TEXT Description: Local political entity that has the authority to adopt and enforce floodplain ordinances for the area under its jurisdiction.
Column name: CURRENT_FLOOD_ZONE Type: TEXT Description: Flood zone derived from the Flood Insurance Rate Map (FIRM) where the insured property is currently located.
Column name: ZIP_GEO_ID Type: TEXT Description: Cybersyn's unique identifier for a zip code, joinable to GEOGRAPHY_INDEX.
Column name: OBSTRUCTION Type: TEXT Description: Type of obstruction in the enclosure of the insured property.
Column name: LOWEST_FLOOR_ELEVATION Type: FLOAT Description: A building's lowest floor is the floor or level (including basement/enclosure/crawlspace/sub-grade crawlspace) that is used as the point of reference when rating a building. This includes the level to which a building is flood-proofed. The elevation in feet of the reference level of the building from the Elevation Certificate.
Column name: CONDOMINIUM_COVERAGE_TYPE Type: TEXT Description: Type of coverage the building has if it is a condominium.
Column name: ADDITIONAL_BUILDING_RATE Type: FLOAT Description: Additional building rate selected by the company. This data element must be reported for all policies except the Preferred Risk Policy (PRP).
Column name: CONTENT_LOCATION Type: TEXT Description: The location of the contents of the property.
Column name: MAP_PANEL_SUFFIX Type: TEXT Description: Either the current map panel suffix for the property or the map panel suffix used for rating, depending on MapInfo Type.
Column name: ORIGINAL_CONSTRUCTION_DATE Type: DATE Description: Original date of the construction of the building.
Sample rows:
[{'NATIONAL_FLOOD_INSURANCE_PROGRAM_POLICY_ID': 'c3ade445-7e4b-4e1a-8b57-94f54a173b77', 'BUILDING_TYPE': 'Main House', 'OCCUPANCY_TYPE': 'Single family residence', 'TOTAL_BUILDING_INSURANCE_COVERAGE': 250000, 'BUILDING_DEDUCTIBLE': 1250, 'TOTAL_CONTENTS_INSURANCE_COVERAGE': 100000, 'CONTENTS_DEDUCTIBLE': 1250.0, 'TOTAL_INSURANCE_PREMIUM_OF_THE_POLICY': 348, 'POLICY_COST': 450.0, 'POLICY_COUNT': 1, 'BUILDING_REPLACEMENT_COST': 196640, 'INSURANCE_TO_VALUE_RATIO': '.75 or more', 'PROPERTY_INDICATORS': '[\n  "1 year term",\n  "Post-FIRM Construction",\n  "Primary Residence of the Insured",\n  "NFIP Regular Program"\n]', 'BASIC_BUILDING_RATE': 0.0, 'BASIC_CONTENTS_RATE': 0.0, 'ADDITIONAL_BUILDING_RATE': 0.0, 'ADDITIONAL_CONTENTS_RATE': 0.0, 'PROBATION_SURCHARGE': 0.0, 'FEDERAL_POLICY_FEE': 25, 'HFIAA_SURCHARGE': 25, 'ICC_PREMIUM': 4, 'POLICY_RATING_METHOD': 'Preferred Risk Policy (within a non-SFHA)', 'SUBSIDIZATION_TYPE': 'Not subsidized', 'WAITING_PERIOD_TYPE': 'No waiting period', 'ORIGI


