Table full name: WEATHER__ENVIRONMENT.CYBERSYN.FEMA_DISASTER_DECLARATION_AREAS_INDEX
Column name: STATE_GEO_ID Type: TEXT Description: Cybersyn's unique identifier for a state, joinable to GEOGRAPHY_INDEX.
Column name: DECLARED_PROGRAMS_DETAILED Type: ARRAY Description: Array of programs that were declared for the disaster to provide assistance.
Column name: FEMA_REGION_ID Type: NUMBER Description: The FEMA Region number.
Column name: DESIGNATED_DATE Type: DATE Description: The date a disaster was officially designated.
Column name: DISASTER_DECLARATION_RECORD_ID Type: TEXT Description: Unique record identifier from FEMA for a disaster and an associated impacted geography.
Column name: FEMA_PLACE_CODE Type: TEXT Description: A unique code system FEMA uses internally to recognize locations that takes the numbers '99' + the 3-digit county FIPS code. There are some declared locations that dont have recognized FIPS county codes in which case a unique identifier is assigned.
Column name: ENTRY_DATE Type: DATE Description: The date the disaster areas were first entered into the NEMIS system.
Column name: DISASTER_ID Type: TEXT Description: Sequentially FEMA-assigned number used to designate an event or incident declared as a disaster.
Column name: FEMA_DESIGNATED_AREA Type: TEXT Description: The name or phrase describing the geographic area that was included in the declaration
Column name: TRIBAL_REQUEST Type: BOOLEAN Description: Denotes that a declaration request was submitted directly to the President, independently of a state, by a Tribal Nation.
Column name: CLOSEOUT_DATE Type: DATE Description: The official closeout date of a disaster, after which, one can no longer apply for assistance.
Column name: COUNTY_GEO_ID Type: TEXT Description: Cybersyn's unique identifier for a county, joinable to GEOGRAPHY_INDEX.
Column name: UPDATE_DATE Type: DATE Description: The date the disaster areas were last updated by NEMIS.
